    {
      "id": "is-looping",
      "name": "IsLooping",
      "category": "AnimBank",
      "signature": "IsLooping(Target)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "UAnimBank*"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Bool",
      "docs": "Note: This is almost fully conservative, but since it is derived from\nbone positions on the skeleton (not skinning all verts across all frames)\nit could have some edge cases for (presumably) strange content.\nThis hasn't been an issue in practice yet, so we won't worry about it,\nand each anim bank sequence has an optional BoundsScale that can be adjusted\nto account for certain cases that might fail.\nOne possible future idea if needed, is to calculate a per-bone influence radius\nin the skeleton mesh build, where each bone has a bounding sphere of all weighted\nvertex positions. Then we could try something like the following to make the\nbounds possibly fit this content better.\nInitialAnimatedBoundsMin(AssetBounds.Origin - AssetBounds.BoxExtent);\nInitialAnimatedBoundsMax(AssetBounds.Origin + AssetBounds.BoxExtent);\nFor each Key,Bone:\nAnimatedBoundsMin = Min(AnimatedBoundsMin, InitialAnimatedBoundsMin + Bone.Pos[Key] - Bone.RefPos)\nAnimatedBoundsMax = Max(AnimatedBoundsMax, InitialAnimatedBoundsMax + Bone.Pos[Key] - Bone.RefPos)"
    },
